# Task Manager API

Task Manager API is a backend REST API built with Java 17, Spring Boot, Spring Data JPA and PostgreSQL.

The application supports task CRUD operations, filtering by status and title, request validation, 
global exception handling, and Swagger/OpenAPI documentation.

## Technologies

- Java 17
- Spring Boot
- Spring Data JPA
- PostgreSQL
- Maven
- Lombok
- Validation
- DTO / Mapper
- Swagger / OpenAPI
- Git / GitHub

## Features

- Create task
- Get all tasks
- Get task by ID
- Update task
- Delete task
- Search tasks by status
- Search tasks by title
- Validation
- DTO mapping between entities and API responses
- Global exception handling

## API Endpoints

- GET `/tasks`
- GET `/tasks/{id}`
- GET `/tasks/status/{status}`
- GET `/tasks/title/{title}`
- POST `/tasks`
- PUT `/tasks/{id}`
- DELETE `/tasks/{id}`

## Task Status

Available statuses:

- NEW
- IN_PROGRESS
- DONE

## Project Structure

Controller → Service → Repository → PostgreSQL

## Swagger

After starting the application, Swagger UI is available at:

`http://localhost:8080/swagger-ui/index.html`

